
  Rebase each worktree onto its parent, the branch it was created from, parents before children:
  origin is fetched once, the branches rebased onto but not rebased (the base branch among them)
  are fast-forwarded to origin first, then each worktree is rebased in turn, after catching up
  with its own branch on origin. Without arguments, the wizard asks which worktrees to sync, those
  that need it checked; unattended, those that need it are synced. A worktree is named by its
  branch or its path; --all asks for every worktree.

  By default the worktrees under each one named are synced too, and the plan names each of them;
  --descendants=false syncs the named alone. --ff-parents=false rebases onto the parents as they
  stand.

  A rebase that stops on a conflict is aborted, the worktree left as it was, and the worktrees
  under it are skipped; --keep-conflict leaves it in progress to resolve, then sync it again to
  sync what is left. --push force-pushes each branch synced, leasing on origin's branch as fetched.

  A worktree in the middle of a rebase, a bisect or a merge, whose directory is gone, whose parent
  is gone or leads back to it, or on whose branch origin has commits it never held is left as it
  is, with what moves it on.

  A worktree with uncommitted changes is unsafe: named, it refuses the whole run before anything
  moves, unless --force, which stashes its changes around the rebase; not named, it is kept as it
  is, with the line that forces it. --force lifts that refusal only: it still asks to confirm,
  unless --yes.

  Usage:
    wtm-next sync [worktree...] [flags]

  Examples:
    # Pick the worktrees to sync
    wtm sync

    # A worktree and every worktree under it
    wtm sync feat/login

    # That worktree alone
    wtm sync feat/login --descendants=false

    # Every worktree, then force-push them, no prompts
    wtm sync --all --push --yes

    # See the plan first, then apply exactly that plan
    wtm sync feat/login --dry-run
    wtm sync feat/login --expect-fingerprint <hash>

    # For a script or an agent, with the v2 JSON envelope
    wtm sync --all --yes --output json

  Flags:
        --all                         Sync every worktree; one with uncommitted changes is left as it is unless --force
        --ask                         Ask again the questions this repository remembers an answer to, to change or forget it
        --descendants                 Sync the worktrees under those named too (default true)
    -n, --dry-run                     Show the plan and its fingerprint, apply nothing
        --expect-fingerprint string   Apply only if the facts still have this fingerprint, the one --dry-run printed
        --ff-parents                  Fast-forward the branches rebased onto but not rebased, the base among them, to origin first (default true)
        --force                       Rebase a worktree that has uncommitted changes, stashed around the rebase
    -h, --help                        help for sync
        --keep-conflict               Leave a rebase that stops on a conflict in progress, to resolve, instead of aborting it; the worktrees under it are skipped either way
        --no-fetch                    Read origin's branches as last fetched
        --output string               Output format: text or json (default "text")
        --push                        Force-push each branch synced to origin, leasing on origin's branch as fetched
    -y, --yes                         Run unattended: no question, no confirmation (without worktrees, those that need a sync; the worktrees under those named come too; nothing is pushed unless --push; a worktree named with uncommitted changes still refuses the run unless --force)

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

